cific disease, similar to the grey-area 'convulsive disorders' example. 'human' is excluded as an organism term, but this phrase is a possible disease class mention and is included.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Disease Class); 11. grey area terms\",\"excluded\":\"no\"},{\"start\":212,\"end\":225,\"text\":\"renal failure\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"'renal failure' is a disease mention that covers a family of more specific kidney failure conditions (acute, chronic), so it is a Disease Class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Disease Class)\",\"excluded\":\"no\"},{\"start\":228,\"end\":246,\"text\":\"intersex disorders\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"'intersex disorders' refers to a family of conditions with multiple specific diseases, so it is a Disease Class mention.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Disease Class)\",\"excluded\":\"no\"},{\"start\":251,\"end\":263,\"text\":\"Wilms tumour\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Wilms tumour is a single specific disease (nephroblastoma). It is annotated as a Specific Disease in this context.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions\",\"excluded\":\"no\"},{\"start\":310,\"end\":318,\"text\":\"syndrome\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"'syndrome' in 'this syndrome' refers to Denys-Drash syndrome, but on its own it is a general term and is excluded from annotation.\",\"guideline_section\":\"4. Do not annotate general terms\",\"excluded\":\"yes\"},{\"start\":374,\"end\":386,\"text\":\"Wilms tumour\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"Wilms tumour is a disease name modifying the noun 'suppressor gene' in 'Wilms tumour suppressor gene'. It is a disease mention used as a modifier, so it is annotated.\",\"guideline_section\":\"3. Annotate disease mentions that are used as Modifiers for other concepts\",\"excluded\":\"no\"}]}", "type